  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* A1 (cont). Laurent structure at P and P' for Lambda = [3,2,0]: (i) the S2 double-pole scalar c2 (prediction lambda2 (lambda1+1) = 8), (ii) the S3 triple pole (prediction: absent), S2(inf) = e2(zeta), S3(inf) = e3(zeta), (iii) the six non-scalar data (H1, H2, S3c[s,1], S3c[s,2]) and which are scalar, (iv) the D2 relation S3c[s,1] = c S3c[s,2] (H_s - S3c[s,2]): the exact c per site at P, P' and further theta2 (Laurent fits with the alternative sample points uSamAlt, which avoid u = theta1 = 3/7 = u0), then the candidate list c in {1/4, 1/3, 1/5, 1/6, 1/8, 1/(l1+1), 1/|Lambda|}. *)\nck = <||>;\nuSamAlt = {5/13, -7/9, 8/11, 4/9, -5/6, 9/7, 11/3, 7/5, -5/2};\nLAP = laurent[DiagonalMatrix[zP], thN]; LAQ = laurent[DiagonalMatrix[zQ], thN];\nscal[a_] := Normal[a][[1, 1]];\ne2f[zz_] := zz[[1]] zz[[2]] + zz[[1]] zz[[3]] + zz[[2]] zz[[3]];\nck[\"S2 double-pole coefficients c2 (s = 1, 2) at P and P'; prediction lambda2 (lambda1 + 1)\"] = {Table[scal[LA[\"S2dbl\"][[s]]], {s, 2}], Table[scal[LAQ[\"S2dbl\"][[s]]], {s, 2}], Λ[[2]] (Λ[[1]] + 1)};\nck[\"S2 double poles are scalars (P, P')\"] = {Table[scalarQ[LA[\"S2dbl\"][[s]]], {s, 2}], Table[scalarQ[LAQ[\"S2dbl\"][[s]]], {s, 2}]};\nck[\"S3 triple poles S3c[s,3] are exactly 0 (s = 1, 2) at P, P'\"] = {Table[zeroQ[LA[\"S3c\"][{s, 3}]], {s, 2}], Table[zeroQ[LAQ[\"S3c\"][{s, 3}]], {s, 2}]};\nck[\"S2(inf) = e2(zeta), S3(inf) = e3(zeta) at P and P' (exact)\"] = {scal[LA[\"S2inf\"]] === e2f[zP], scal[LA[\"S3inf\"]] === Times @@ zP, scal[LAQ[\"S2inf\"]] === e2f[zQ], scal[LAQ[\"S3inf\"]] === Times @@ zQ};\nck[\"the six non-scalar Laurent data at P: is the operator a scalar? H1, H2, S3c[1,1], S3c[1,2], S3c[2,1], S3c[2,2]\"] = scalarQ /@ {LA[\"Hres\"][[1]], LA[\"Hres\"][[2]], LA[\"S3c\"][{1, 1}], LA[\"S3c\"][{1, 2}], LA[\"S3c\"][{2, 1}], LA[\"S3c\"][{2, 2}]};\n(* the D2 relation: c from one nonzero component of the vector (S3c[s,2] (H_s - S3c[s,2])) v, then exact verification as an operator identity *)\nvTest = Table[(-1)^k (k + 2)/7, {k, d2}];\nrelC[LAx_, s_] := Module[{Hs = LAx[\"Hres\"][[s]], a = LAx[\"S3c\"][{s, 2}], b = LAx[\"S3c\"][{s, 1}], q, qv, bv, pos, c},\n  q = a . (Hs - a); qv = Normal[q . vTest]; bv = Normal[b . vTest]; pos = First[Flatten[Position[qv, x_ /; x =!= 0]]]; c = bv[[pos]]/qv[[pos]];\n  {c, zeroQ[b - c q]}];\nck[\"c_Lambda and exact operator identity S3c[s,1] = c S3c[s,2](H_s - S3c[s,2]): {{c, holds} site 1, site 2} at P, then P'\"] = {Table[relC[LA, s], {s, 2}], Table[relC[LAQ, s], {s, 2}]};\nth2v = {-3/5, 1/4, 4/3, -1};\nck[\"same at P for theta2 = -3/5, 1/4, 4/3, -1 (alternative Laurent samples)\"] = Table[Block[{uSam = uSamAlt}, With[{LAt = laurent[gZ, {thN[[1]], t2}]}, Table[relC[LAt, s], {s, 2}]]], {t2, th2v}];\ncands = {1/4, 1/3, 1/5, 1/6, 1/8, 1/(Λ[[1]] + 1), 1/Total[Λ]};\nck[\"candidate c_Lambda in {1/4, 1/3, 1/5, 1/6, 1/8, 1/(l1+1), 1/|Lambda|}: which holds exactly at P (site 1, site 2)\"] = Table[{c, zeroQ[LA[\"S3c\"][{1, 1}] - c LA[\"S3c\"][{1, 2}] . (LA[\"Hres\"][[1]] - LA[\"S3c\"][{1, 2}])], zeroQ[LA[\"S3c\"][{2, 1}] - c LA[\"S3c\"][{2, 2}] . (LA[\"Hres\"][[2]] - LA[\"S3c\"][{2, 2}])]}, {c, cands}];\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"check\", \"result\"}}, List @@@ Normal[ck]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
