   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* A1 (cont). Local exponents of the dual oper (d^3 - S1 d^2 + S2 d - S3) P = 0 at x = u - theta_s read off the chain data: S1 ~ |Lambda|/x, S2 ~ c2/x^2 (the measured scalar double pole), S3 ~ a/x^2 (no triple pole, so S3 does not enter the indicial equation). Indicial polynomial rho (rho-1)(rho-2) - |Lambda| rho (rho-1) + c2 rho. Prediction (P3): exponents {0, l2+1, l1+2} = {0, 3, 5}. Also the general identity c2 = l2 (l1+1) from the exponents. *)\nck = <||>;\nc2meas = scal[LA[\"S2dbl\"][[1]]];\nck[\"measured |Lambda|, c2 (site 1 at P)\"] = {lamTot, c2meas};\nck[\"indicial roots rho of rho[(rho-1)(rho-2) - |Lambda|(rho-1) + c2] = 0 from the measured data\"] = Sort[rho /. Solve[rho ((rho - 1) (rho - 2) - lamTot (rho - 1) + c2meas) == 0, rho]];\nck[\"predicted exponents {0, l2+1, l1+2}\"] = {0, Λ[[2]] + 1, Λ[[1]] + 2};\nck[\"check of the exponent sum |Lambda| + 3 and product (l2+1)(l1+2) = 2 + |Lambda| + c2\"] = {lamTot + 3 === (Λ[[2]] + 1) + (Λ[[1]] + 2), (Λ[[2]] + 1) (Λ[[1]] + 2) === 2 + lamTot + c2meas};\nck[\"the S3 double pole a_s (scalar? value) vs the vacuum-type rule a = c2 omega3 (see the vacuum cell): S3c[s,2] is NOT scalar for the interacting states, only for the vacuum covector\"] = scalarQ[LA[\"S3c\"][{1, 2}]];\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"check\", \"result\"}}, List @@@ Normal[ck]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
