  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task A1. The (inf,inf) vacuum: Omega_D^inf[zeta, om1] = e1 rho(exp(r1 E12) exp(r2 E13) exp(r3 E23)) with the closed forms r_k^inf (the om2 -> infinity limits of the round-1 r_k). Checks: (i) symbolic Limit of rGauss in om2; (ii) exact equality with the Infinity branch of rGauss and numeric closeness at om2 = 10^6, 10^9, 10^12; (iii) what Omega_D depends on (om1, om2 only: om3 drops out - tested by the eigencovector property with several om3); (iv) the rescaled limit operators: the Laurent coefficients of S2, S3 at twist g'(om1, om2, om3) are exact polynomials in om2 (fitted from 5 exact values, 2 checks); Omega^inf (x) Omega^inf must be an eigencovector of the TOP-DEGREE coefficient of each (that is the finite limit of the rescaled operators), and the common eigencovector space of these limit operators is computed exactly. *)\nck = <||>;\nrInf[zz_, w1_] := {(w1 - zz[[1]])/(w1 - zz[[2]]), -((w1 - zz[[1]]) (zz[[2]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]])), ((w1 - zz[[2]]) (zz[[1]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]))};\nΩDinf[zz_, w1_] := coverG[rInf[zz, w1]];\nsymZ = {f1, f2, f3};\nrLim = Table[Limit[rGauss[symZ, o1, o2][[k]], o2 -> Infinity], {k, 3}];\nck[\"(i) Limit[rGauss[zeta, om1, om2], om2 -> Infinity] = r^inf_k (k=1,2,3), symbolic\"] = Together[rLim - rInf[symZ, o1]] === {0, 0, 0};\nck[\"(ii) exact: OmegaDinf = OmegaD[zeta, {om1, Infinity}] (3 points)\"] = Table[ΩDinf[zz, w1] === ΩD[zz, {w1, Infinity}], {zz, {zP, zQ, {-1, 7/3, 1/2}}}, {w1, {5/2, -2/5, 9/7}}];\nck[\"(ii) numeric: |OmegaD[zeta, {om1, 10^k}] - OmegaDinf| / |OmegaDinf| for k = 6, 9, 12 at P, om1 = 5/2 (expect ~ 10^-k)\"] = Table[N[Norm[ΩD[zP, {5/2, 10^k}] - ΩDinf[zP, 5/2]]/Norm[ΩDinf[zP, 5/2]], 4], {k, {6, 9, 12}}];\nck[\"(iii) what OmegaD depends on: the r_k (rGauss) contain om1 and om2 only; symbolic derivative of the Gauss parameters w.r.t. om3 = 0 (om3 never appears)\"] = FreeQ[rGauss[symZ, o1, o2], o3];\n(* eigencovector with twist g'(om1, om2, om3) for om3 varied: OmegaD (x) OmegaD is an exact eigencovector for every om3, hence om3 drops out of the vacuum *)\nom3test = Table[Module[{ww = {5/2, 7/3, w3}, g = gpVar[1][zP, {5/2, 7/3, w3}], O2}, O2 = kron[ΩD[zP, ww[[1 ;; 2]]], ΩD[zP, ww[[1 ;; 2]]]];\n   And @@ Flatten[Table[With[{c = O2 . Sk[k][g, thN, uu]}, Union[Flatten[c - (c[[1]]/O2[[1]]) O2]] === {0}], {k, {2, 3}}, {uu, {u0, u1}}]]], {w3, {3/5, 9/4, -7/3, 11/5}}];\nck[\"(iii) OmegaD (x) OmegaD eigencovector of S2, S3 (u0, u1) at twist g'(5/2, 7/3, om3), om3 = 3/5, 9/4, -7/3, 11/5\"] = om3test;\n(* (iv) rescaled limit: Laurent coefficient operators as exact polynomials in om2 *)\nopKeys = {\"H1\", \"H2\", \"S3c11\", \"S3c12\", \"S3c21\", \"S3c22\"};\nopsW[w2_] := opsW[w2] = With[{L = laurent[gpVar[1][zP, {5/2, w2, 3/5}], thN]}, <|\"H1\" -> L[\"Hres\"][[1]], \"H2\" -> L[\"Hres\"][[2]], \"S3c11\" -> L[\"S3c\"][{1, 1}], \"S3c12\" -> L[\"S3c\"][{1, 2}], \"S3c21\" -> L[\"S3c\"][{2, 1}], \"S3c22\" -> L[\"S3c\"][{2, 2}]|>];\nw2fit = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}; w2chk = {6, 7};\nVandInv = Inverse[Table[w^j, {w, w2fit}, {j, 0, 4}]];\npolyCoef[key_] := Table[Sum[VandInv[[j + 1, k]] opsW[w2fit[[k]]][key], {k, 5}], {j, 0, 4}];\npolyRes[key_, cs_] := Table[And @@ {zeroQ[Sum[w^j cs[[j + 1]], {j, 0, 4}] - opsW[w][key]]}, {w, w2chk}];\npolyData = Association[Table[key -> With[{cs = polyCoef[key]}, <|\"cs\" -> cs, \"res\" -> polyRes[key, cs], \"deg\" -> Max[Select[Range[5], ! zeroQ[cs[[#]]] &]] - 1|>], {key, opKeys}]];\nck[\"(iv) Laurent-coefficient operators are polynomials in om2: {fit residuals zero at om2 = 6, 7; degree in om2} for H1, H2, S3c[1,1], S3c[1,2], S3c[2,1], S3c[2,2]\"] = Table[{key, polyData[key][\"res\"], polyData[key][\"deg\"]}, {key, opKeys}];\ntopOp[key_] := polyData[key][\"cs\"][[polyData[key][\"deg\"] + 1]];\nCinf = kron[ΩDinf[zP, 5/2], ΩDinf[zP, 5/2]];\neigInf = Table[With[{O = topOp[key], c = Cinf . topOp[key]}, {key, polyData[key][\"deg\"], Union[Flatten[c - (c[[1]]/Cinf[[1]]) Cinf]] === {0}, c[[1]]/Cinf[[1]]}], {key, opKeys}];\nck[\"(iv) OmegaDinf (x) OmegaDinf is a left eigencovector of the TOP-degree-in-om2 coefficient of each Laurent operator: {key, degree, eigencovector?, eigenvalue}\"] = eigInf;\n(* the exact common eigencovector space of the limit operators (eigenvalues taken from OmegaDinf) *)\nlimOps = Table[topOp[key], {key, opKeys}];\nlamV = eigInf[[All, 4]];\nstackM = Join @@ Table[Transpose[Normal[limOps[[i]]]] - lamV[[i]] IdentityMatrix[d2], {i, Length[limOps]}];\nnsC = NullSpace[stackM];\nck[\"(iv) dimension of the exact common left-eigencovector space of the limit operators (eigenvalues of OmegaDinf (x) OmegaDinf)\"] = Length[nsC];\nck[\"(iv) the common eigencovector (if 1-dim) is parallel to OmegaDinf (x) OmegaDinf\"] = If[Length[nsC] === 1, MatrixRank[{First[nsC], Cinf}] === 1, \"n/a\"];\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"check\", \"result\"}}, List @@@ Normal[ck], {{\"r^inf_1, r^inf_2, r^inf_3 (closed form)\", ToString[Factor /@ rInf[{z1, z2, z3}, w1], InputForm]}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
