  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* A3 (cont). Is theta12 * (matrix of S3c[1,2] on the exact HW space) exactly theta-independent, i.e. S3c[1,2]|_HW = (1/theta12) * N0 with a fixed matrix N0 and NO scalar part? Exact test over the three theta of the universality cell, for each multiplicity-2 sector; N0, its trace and determinant, eigenvalues, and the coordinate-ratio quadratic M12 r^2 + (M11 - M22) r - M21 = 0 in the HW-ket basis hwKets[mu] (basis dependent); the 3 x 3 differences of theta12 M(theta). *)\nck = <||>;\nn0Data = Table[Module[{rowsMu = Select[c4Rows, #[[1]] === mu &], N0s},\n   N0s = Table[r[[3]] r[[4]], {r, rowsMu}];\n   {mu, Length[Union[N0s]] == 1, First[N0s], Tr[First[N0s]], Det[First[N0s]], N[Eigenvalues[First[N0s]], 15], With[{M = First[N0s]}, M[[1, 2]] r^2 + (M[[1, 1]] - M[[2, 2]]) r - M[[2, 1]]]}], {mu, multSecs}];\nck[\"theta12 * M(theta) identical at the 3 theta (exact) => S3c[1,2]|_HW = N0/theta12, no scalar part: per sector {mu, constant?, N0, trace, det, eigenvalues, ratio quadratic}\"] = n0Data;\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"check\", \"result\"}}, List @@@ Normal[ck]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
