  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "*Printed output of the code cell above (evaluated from exactly the saved source in kernel K1 via Get; not a native notebook output).*\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| time (s) | 0.0206973 |\n| (a) exact undo on all HW kets at 11 points (P, P', 1 generic, 8 regime): {all equal, naive e1 (x) e1-type control differs} | {11, {{True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}}} |\n| (b) closed forms: a', c', g' = b' - a' c' (symbolic in zeta = (f1,f2,f3), om1 = o1, om1' = p1) | {\"-(((-f1 + f2)*(o1 - p1))/((f2 - o1)*(f2 - p1)))\", \"((f1 - f3)*(f2 - f3)*(o1 - p1))/((f1 - f2)*(f3 - o1)*(f3 - p1))\", \"((-f1 + f3)*(-f2 + f3)*(o1 - p1))/((f3 - o1)*(f2 - p1)*(f3 - p1))\"} |\n| (b) eps-free: parameters at (f, o1, p1) -> eps (f, o1, p1) equal the parameters at eps = 1 (symbolic, exact) | True |\n| (b) the XXX factorisation structure: a' = (f2 - f1)(o1 - p1)/((f2 - o1)(f2 - p1))? compare with the round-1 finite-twist a' at om2 = om2' = infinity (symbolic equality) | True |\n| (b) rank of the Jacobian of (oh1, oh1') -> (a', c', g') at 4 generic points (expect 2) | {2, 2, 2, 2} |\n| (b) the three functions (a', c', g') are algebraically dependent? (Jacobian 3x2 so yes); relation test: rank of the 3x3 matrix [grad a', grad c', grad g'] w.r.t. (o1, p1, f1) at a generic point (expect 3 if f1 enters independently) | 3 |\n| controls: om1' = om1 gives n' = 1 exactly (a' = c' = g' = 0) | True |\n| (c) per-weight ranks over the 4-point grid at phi, over 6 points at phi, over 4 points at phi' : {weight, dim, rank4, rank6, rank4(phi'), used as a CG slice weight} | {{{0, 2, 3}, 1, 1, 1, 1, False}, {{0, 3, 2}, 1, 1, 1, 1, False}, {{1, 1, 3}, 1, 1, 1, 1, True}, {{1, 2, 2}, 2, 2, 2, 2, True}, {{1, 3, 1}, 1, 1, 1, 1, False}, {{2, 0, 3}, 1, 1, 1, 1, False}, {{2, 1, 2}, 2, 2, 2, 2, True}, {{2, 2, 1}, 2, 2, 2, 2, True}, {{2, 3, 0}, 1, 1, 1, 1, True}, {{3, 0, 2}, 1, 1, 1, 1, True}, {{3, 1, 1}, 1, 1, 1, 1, True}, {{3, 2, 0}, 1, 1, 1, 1, True}} |\n| (c) CG-complete on the slice weights used (rank = dim with the 4-point grid) | True |\n| (c) CG-complete on EVERY weight of V (rank = dim with the 4-point grid; with the 6-point grid) | {True, True} |\n| (c) regression: phi_u(grid, 4 points) = coverG[{a', g', c'}] from the closed forms (exact) | True |",
