   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* B3 prelude: DERIVATION of the quadratic relation of D2 (the closed form verified exactly in the next cell). Among the 8 generators {id, W, H1, S3c12, S3c11, H1.H1, H1.S3c12, S3c12.S3c12} (site 1, basis 1) the exact null space of the operator sketches is one-dimensional at every (zeta, theta2) tried; normalised to the coefficient 1 of S3c11 it is {c_id, c_W, c_H1, c_S3c12, 1, c_HH, c_HS, c_SS}. (i) the quadratic part (c_HH, c_HS, c_SS) is constant; (ii) zeta-dependence at theta2 = -3/5: each of c_W, c_H1, c_S3c12, c_id fitted by a quadratic polynomial in zeta (10 monomials from 10 random zeta, residual on 4 more); (iii) theta12-dependence at zeta = P: each coefficient fitted by a polynomial in 1/theta12 of degree 2 (5 of the 9 theta2 values, residual on the other 4). *)\nck = <||>;\nnm1 = bNames[1]; pos1[n_] := Position[nm1, n][[1, 1]];\ngens8 = {\"id\", \"W\", \"H1\", \"S3c12\", \"S3c11\", \"H1.H1\", \"H1.S3c12\", \"S3c12.S3c12\"};\nrelAt[zz_, th2_] := Module[{sc = bSetup[zz, wP, {thN[[1]], th2}, 1], ns}, ns = NullSpace[Transpose[sc[\"Sk\"][[pos1 /@ gens8]]]]; If[Length[ns] == 1, First[ns]/ns[[1, 5]], ns]];\nSeedRandom[5];\nzpts = Table[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 3]/RandomInteger[{2, 7}, 3] + {1/11, 1/13, 1/17}, {14}];\nrelZ = Table[{z, relAt[z, -3/5]}, {z, zpts}];\nquadB = {1, z1, z2, z3, z1^2, z2^2, z3^2, z1 z2, z1 z3, z2 z3};\nfitZ[k_] := Module[{cf = LinearSolve[Table[quadB /. Thread[{z1, z2, z3} -> r[[1]]], {r, relZ[[1 ;; 10]]}], relZ[[1 ;; 10, 2, k]]]}, {cf . quadB, Max[Abs[Table[cf . (quadB /. Thread[{z1, z2, z3} -> r[[1]]]) - r[[2, k]], {r, relZ[[11 ;; 14]]}]]]}];\nck[\"(i) the relation is unique (1-dim null space) and its quadratic part (c_HH, c_HS, c_SS) is the same at all 14 zeta points\"] = {And @@ (Length[#[[2]]] == 8 & /@ relZ), Union[relZ[[All, 2, 6 ;; 8]]]};\nck[\"(ii) zeta-dependence at theta12 = 31/35: {fit polynomial, max residual at 4 further zeta} for c_W, c_H1, c_S3c12, c_id (in this order)\"] = {fitZ[2], fitZ[3], fitZ[4], fitZ[1]};\nth2s9 = {-3/5, 1/4, -1, 4/3, 5/7, 2, -4/3, 7/5, 3};\nrelT = Table[{1/(thN[[1]] - t2), relAt[zP, t2]}, {t2, th2s9}];\nfitT[k_] := Module[{cf = LinearSolve[Table[{1, x, x^2} /. x -> r[[1]], {r, relT[[1 ;; 3]]}], relT[[1 ;; 3, 2, k]]]}, {cf . {1, x, x^2}, Max[Abs[Table[cf . {1, r[[1]], r[[1]]^2} - r[[2, k]], {r, relT[[4 ;; 9]]}]]]}];\nck[\"(iii) theta12-dependence at zeta = P: coefficient as a polynomial in x = 1/theta12 (fit on 3 theta2, residual on 6 more), c_W, c_H1, c_S3c12, c_id; at P: s = Sum zeta = 41/12, e2(zeta) = 89/24\"] = {fitT[2], fitT[3], fitT[4], fitT[1]};\nck[\"quadratic part at the 9 theta2 (constant?)\"] = Union[relT[[All, 2, 6 ;; 8]]];\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"check\", \"result\"}}, List @@@ Normal[ck]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "*Printed output of the code cell above (evaluated from exactly the saved source in kernel K1 via Get; not a native notebook output).*\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| check | result |\n| (i) the relation is unique (1-dim null space) and its quadratic part (c_HH, c_HS, c_SS) is the same at all 14 zeta points | {True, {{-3, 7/4, -1/4}}} |\n| (ii) zeta-dependence at theta12 = 31/35: {fit polynomial, max residual at 4 further zeta} for c_W, c_H1, c_S3c12, c_id (in this order) | {{105/31, 0}, {2730/31 + 15*z1 + 15*z2 + 15*z3, 0}, {-1575/62 - (9*z1)/2 - (9*z2)/2 - (9*z3)/2, 0}, {-617400/961 - (7350*z1)/31 - 18*z1^2 - (7350*z2)/31 - 39*z1*z2 - 18*z2^2 - (7350*z3)/31 - 39*z1*z3 - 39*z2*z3 - 18*z3^2, 0}} |\n| (iii) theta12-dependence at zeta = P: coefficient as a polynomial in x = 1/theta12 (fit on 3 theta2, residual on 6 more), c_W, c_H1, c_S3c12, c_id; at P: s = Sum zeta = 41/12, e2(zeta) = 89/24 | {{3*x, 0}, {205/4 + 78*x, 0}, {-123/8 - (45*x)/2, 0}, {-885/4 - (1435*x)/2 - 504*x^2, 0}} |\n| quadratic part at the 9 theta2 (constant?) | {{-3, 7/4, -1/4}} |",
   "languageId": "markdown",
