lean S3c[s,1] = c S3c[s,2](H_s − S3c[s,2]); its quadratic part is 12H² − 7Ha + a² = (3H − a)(4H − a). (iii) The fourth localiser keeps its shape; only the W coefficient changes (2 → 1). (iv) The dual sectors' θ₁₂S3c12 eigenvalues are shifted by a sector-dependent scalar. (v) The (inf,inf) family's σ₂ for the multiplicity-1 sector (4,4,2) is small (3e-4 .. 7e-4) for the chosen grid pairs. (vi) The exact slice of (4,4,2) has an exactly vanishing component and the sign convention of the HW kets differs between the exact ket and the chain branch for it; the CG cells here align the sign of the exact slice with the chain slice and use norm-based errors (the round-2 elementwise errors would have divided by zero and shown 2.0 for this branch).\n\n**Not done.** Q-side rows (direct oper gauge, degrees, Wronskians, det N, jet formula, P′ = κP statements): P4. The Λ-dependence of the X₄ W coefficient needs a third representation. The fit of the D2 relation coefficients (cells 63-64) assumes polynomial structure in (ζ, 1/θ₁₂) read off at fixed θ and fixed ζ respectively; the exact identity is verified at 6 combined (ζ,θ) points (cell 66). The spectator f₄ of v₄ is a θ₁₂-independent constant (−55995289/138911112 at P); no closed form was attempted. Timing: the localising-scan cell 59 takes about 6 min in a cold kernel (two scans plus cubic spans), cell 61 about 66 s; everything else is below 10 s. No native outputs are stored (rerun in VS Code to store them); final cell count 75.",
